# WIN-INSTALL-CONTRACT-MAP — POSIX to Windows compatibility map

File: openOODA/audit/win_install_contract_map.oot
Sibling 1 of 3 from win_install_contract.oot. See:
- win_install_contract.oot — §0-3, active install path audit
- win_install_contract_phase4.oot — §7-10, Phase 4 contract + open Qs

Date: 2026-08-19. Lane owner: cli (Windows variant is cli territory).
This file holds the POSIX->Windows compat map for shell commands, file paths,
and the BOOTSTRAP_PIN status. It is the mechanical reference for whoever
writes `install_win.oo`.

## 4. shell command map

Used by `install_xdg.oo` (active path):

| POSIX | Purpose | Windows replacement | Caveats |
|---|---|---|---|
| `test -x <path>` | Check binary is executable | `if exist <path>` (cmd) or `Test-Path <path>` (ps) | Windows uses file extension (`PATHEXT`) for executability, not the `+x` bit. Skip the bit check. |
| `mkdir -p <p1 p2 ...>` | Create dirs | `mkdir <p1> <p2> ...` (cmd, no flag) | `mkdir` in cmd is recursive by default since Vista. ps: `New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path <p>`. |
| `cp -f <src> <dst>` | Copy file, overwrite | `copy /Y <src> <dst>` (cmd) or `Copy-Item -Force <src> <dst>` (ps) | `/Y` suppresses the overwrite prompt. |
| `cp -a <src> <dst>` | Copy tree, preserve attrs | `robocopy <src> <dst> /E /COPY:DATSO /NFL /NDL /NJH /NJS /NP /R:0 /W:0` | `cp -a` is recursive + preserves mode/owner/timestamps. `robocopy /E /COPY:DATSO` is the closest. Or `xcopy /E /I /K /X /Y`. |
| `chmod +x <paths>` | Mark executable | **No-op** on Windows | Executability is by extension. Don't fail the install on this. |
| `rm -rf <path>` | Recursive delete | `rmdir /S /Q <path>` (cmd) or `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force <path>` (ps) | The std/runtime slot wipe at `install_xdg.oo:71,79` is best-effort already; on Windows keep it best-effort. |
| `printf '\033[<code>m'` (in `install_art.oo:13`) | ANSI color | Same. | Windows 10+ conhost and modern Terminal handle VT. Enable with `chcp 65001` and VT mode. cmd needs `set TERM=`. Or skip ink on Windows and use plain `println`. |

Used by residual `chapters_a.oo`:

| POSIX | Purpose | Windows replacement | Caveats |
|---|---|---|---|
| `http_download(net, url, path)` | HTTPS GET | `Invoke-WebRequest -Uri <url> -OutFile <path>` (ps) or `curl.exe` (Win 10 1803+) | `NetCap` semantics must be preserved. |
| `extract_tar_gz(sys, tar, dir)` | Unpack `.tar.gz` | `tar -xzf <tar> -C <dir>` (Win 10 1803+ bsdtar) or `Expand-Archive` for `.zip` only | The release ships `.tar.gz`; `Expand-Archive` won't do it. Use bsdtar. |
| `mkdir_p(fs, path)` | Capability mkdir | Already a runtime capability | Cross-platform if the runtime provides it. |
| `copy_file(fs, src, dst)` | Capability copy | Already a runtime capability | Same. |
| `chmod_exec(fs, path)` | Set +x | Should be a no-op on Windows | Same. |
| `sys_exec(sys, bin, "--version")` | Probe binary | `sys_exec` must work on Windows; needs `cmd /c <bin>.exe --version` or equivalent | Capability layer concern, not install. |

## 5. file path map

`install_xdg.oo` paths (active) - POSIX -> Windows:

| POSIX | Windows |
|---|---|
| `~/.local/bin/ooda` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\bin\ooda.exe` |
| `~/.local/bin/oodac` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\bin\oodac.exe` |
| `~/.local/bin/oo` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\bin\oo.bat` (cmd shim) or skip |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/std/` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\std\` |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/runtime/` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\runtime\` |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/oodac/oodac` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\oodac\oodac.exe` |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/share/fixtures/hello.oo` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\share\fixtures\hello.oo` |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/share/INSTALL_RECEIPT.txt` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\share\INSTALL_RECEIPT.txt` |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/install/` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\install\` |
| `~/.local/share/ooda/share/` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\data\share\` |
| `~/.config/ooda/env` | `%APPDATA%\openooda\env.bat` (or `env.ps1`) |
| `~/.cache/ooda/` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\cache\` |
| `~/.cache/ooda/downloads/` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\cache\downloads\` |

The two trees are **separate** on POSIX (data vs config) and should stay
separate on Windows (`%LOCALAPPDATA%` for data+cache+bin, `%APPDATA%` for
config). Do **not** collapse them into one `%USERPROFILE%\openooda`.

**Path-separator trap.** `install_xdg.oo` builds paths with `/`:
`home_user + "/.local/share/ooda"`. Windows `process_exec` will choke on
`mkdir "C:\Users\j\AppData\Local\openooda\data/bin/ooda"`. The Windows
install must build paths with `\` (or use a `path_join` helper) and quote
them for cmd.

**Reserved Windows path chars.** `Path.ContainsAny("\0")` aside, the
literal strings here (`ooda`, `oodac`, `share`, `fixtures`, `env`,
`INSTALL_RECEIPT.txt`) are clean. The install user-names the write root,
so the only reserved-char risk is the `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` value itself -
defense should refuse any path containing `;`, `&`, `|`, `<`, `>`, `^`, `"`.

## 6. BOOTSTRAP_PIN status

File: `openOODA/ooda/install/BOOTSTRAP_PIN` (1 line, content: `v0.205.0-beta`).

- **Current pin** (per `openOODA/START.oot` and the user profile): `v0.205.0-beta`.
- **Pin in BOOTSTRAP_PIN**: `v0.205.0-beta`.
- **Status**: **Correct.** Match.

**Hardcoded pin in `install_xdg.oo:110`:**
`"version=v0.205.0-beta\n"` in the receipt string. This is a hand-mirror of
BOOTSTRAP_PIN. A Windows variant should mirror the same pin (or read it from
`BOOTSTRAP_PIN` and write it into the receipt).

**How a Windows install fetches the matching version.** The active path does
**not** fetch - it copies from `OODA_CHECKOUT`. So a Windows install is
checkout-driven: the user must clone `https://github.com/openOODA/ooda` at the
desired tag, rebuild oodac, and then run install. The Windows git equivalent
is Git for Windows (`git.exe`) or WSL. Tag checkout: `git clone ... && cd ooda
&& git checkout v0.205.0-beta`. The `BOOTSTRAP_PIN` file ships inside the
checkout; the Windows install should read it and write the pin into the
receipt and `INSTALL_RECEIPT.txt`. The active `install_xdg.oo` writes a
literal `v0.205.0-beta` instead - that is a residual hardcode; a Windows
rewrite should fix both paths.

See `win_install_contract_phase4.oot` for the Phase 4 minimum and maximum
contract and what was not checked.
